# Data -- 233MB, exceeds GitHub's 100MB hard file-size limit and isn't suited to git
# history anyway (never actually shrinks a repo once committed, even after deletion).
# Place Business_Report.csv at the repo root manually; see CLAUDE.md for the schema.
Business_Report.csv

# Secrets / local environment overrides. .env currently ships only default values (see
# CLAUDE.md) so committing it has never been *unsafe* so far, but that's exactly the kind
# of thing that quietly stops being true the first time someone adds a real credential --
# .env.example (committed) documents the same fields without that risk.
.env

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Runtime output -- app/core/logging_config.py recreates logs/ on startup either way.
logs/
*.log

# Editor/OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Documents -- the process-spec PDF and anything else. *.pdf matches at every
# directory level, not just the repo root.
*.pdf

# Generated EDA reports -- sweetviz output built from the real transaction data, so
# they embed live agent names and volume distributions. Regenerate on demand with
# `python eda/generate_eda_report.py`; the generator itself stays in the repo.
eda/*.html
I*.pdf

# business notes
busi*.py

# Test artifacts (.pytest_cache/ already covered above)
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Notebooks
*.ipynb

# Editor workspace settings -- machine-specific paths and personal preferences, not
# project configuration. .vscode/ appeared as untracked before the first push.
.vscode/
.idea/

# Scratch/QA output produced while testing, never part of the deliverable.
qa_report.html
*.orig
*.rej

# Colab-exported prototype (business_data_send.py and friends) -- kept locally as
# reference for where the safety-stock / gap-analysis terminology came from, but not
# part of the deliverable; app/ generalises it.
business*.py
